<%#
  A forecast panel body — the only part that slides. The silver bars, green
  header, and footer are fixed chrome rendered once in locations/show. Used as a
  partial layout:
    render layout: "locations/panels/frame", locals: { key: } do ... end
  The title comes from ForecastsHelper::PANELS, the one list that also fixes the
  panels' order; data-title feeds the fixed header + silver-bar labels via the
  forecast controller.

  The id is what pins each panel when a refresh morphs new readings in: the
  stats strip drops blank tiles, so two renders of the same panel can differ in
  shape, and without an id to match on the morph is left guessing which sibling
  is which.
%>
<div class="wii-panel-body" id="panel_<%= key %>"
  data-panel="<%= key %>" data-title="<%= panel_title(key) %>" data-forecast-target="panel">
  <%= yield %>
</div>
